  "long_description": "Walking accomplished far less useful distance and carried greater cumulative dynamic shock per useful mile than Mall, PT, and FNS/SNS skating in the displayed established summaries. Walking may show lower total burden because the activity ended after very little mobility. The functional comparison is the burden required to accomplish useful movement. Distance denominators and sample counts remain explicit; unequal exposure is not hidden. N-of-1 case study example This N-of-1 case study example illustrates a review method and is not universal. Canonical case evidence: https://handicapskater.com/evidence/mobility-comparison/ Wearables estimate physiologic, autonomic, MSK, movement, impact, and transport burden. They do not directly measure pain. Results are N-of-1 evidence, not clinical proof, diagnosis, causation, universal proof, or legal proof.",
